From: Cody McGinnis <brainwart@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo, qmp-usb: gate clocks in system suspend

The QMP USB PHYs only gate their aux, ref and pipe clocks, and only enter
autonomous (wakeup detection) mode, from their runtime suspend callbacks.
They have no system sleep callbacks.

During system suspend the PHYs stay runtime active: the PM core holds a
usage reference from prepare, the controllers are runtime-resumed by
usb_suspend() to switch root hub wakeup, and the xHCI roothub keeps its
own phy_power_on() reference until bus suspend. The aux clocks hang off
the RPMh XO clock (bi_tcxo), so the APPS XO vote stays on through s2idle
and the SoC never reaches XO shutdown (AOSD) or DDR self-refresh.

On a ThinkPad X13s, tracing clk_prepare/clk_unprepare up to
machine_suspend showed gcc_usb3_{prim,sec,mp}_phy_aux_clk_src as the only
users of bi_tcxo left prepared.

Force the runtime suspend path in the late system suspend phase, after
the controllers have suspended, and undo it in the early resume phase.
This is the same state the PHYs are in when the controller is runtime
suspended with remote wakeup armed.
---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4466,6 +4466,8 @@
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_combo_pm_ops = {
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_combo_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	SET_LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+				     pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static int qmp_combo_reset_init(struct qmp_combo *qmp)
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
@@ -2153,6 +2153,8 @@
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_usb_pm_ops = {
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_usb_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_usb_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	SET_LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+				     pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static int qmp_usb_reset_init(struct qmp_usb *qmp,
